; A QUALIFIED reference to a private macro. Bare `privMac` has drawn
; AX3023 since visibility landed; the qualified spelling drew a false
; AX3001 until 2026-08-14, because nothing split `VisAll$privMac`
; against the macro table's bare names - the same wrong answer
; qualified private types used to get, fixed the same way
; (`declMatches`' rule). docs/macro-system.md MAC-LANG-12.
(import VisAll)
(:: main Int)
(fn (main) (VisAll::privMac 2))
